! Read by SIS2 after SIS_input and the domain's SIS_override, and it holds what
! the *forcing source* implies about the model rather than what the domain does.
!
! Shared by every real source because every real source is sub-daily. It is a
! separate file, and not a line in the domain's SIS_override, because that file
! carries NIGLOBAL and NJGLOBAL: folding this into it would mean one copy per
! (domain, source) pair to say the same sentence.

! ADD_DIURNAL_SW synthesizes a diurnal cycle from the shortwave it is handed, on
! the assumption that the value is a daily mean. Every source ACKBAR archives
! reports shortwave at least three hourly, so with it left on the cycle is
! applied twice: the model runs to completion, reports success, and puts a
! diurnal amplitude on the sea surface that no atmosphere asked for.
#override ADD_DIURNAL_SW = False
